            <ArticleTitle>Craniomandibular osteopathy in a bullmastiff.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>883-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 6-month-old bullmastiff was presented with bilateral painful swellings of the mandible. Craniomandibular osteopathy was diagnosed based on skull radiographs and histological findings from bone biopsies. Treatment consisted of meloxicam to alleviate the pain. Three months later, the dog was pain free without medication or palpable change in the mandible.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
